### 1. Architectural Explanation of Vulnerability & Mechanical Resolution

The adversarial audit established a verified **SV-2 (Critical)** systemic deadlock under sub-threshold, non-attributable siege conditions:

1. **High-Entropy Capital Depletion (Art. 3.5.2 & Art. 6.1.2):**
   - *Vulnerability:* Article 3.5.2 strictly mandated reserves of low-entropy primary biological resources (grain, potable water, medical biomass) for 12–24 months. It completely ignored non-biological, high-complexity components (photolithographic power semiconductors, high-efficiency polyamide reverse-osmosis membranes, high-voltage vacuum switchgear, sub-station capacitor banks). When severed from global Track-A supply chains and subject to covert friction, local open-source fabrication commons (Art. 6.3.2) lacked the cleanroom precision or toolmaker-level capital to fabricate these high-entropy spare parts on demand.
   - *Mechanical Fix:* Art. 3.5.2 and Art. 6.1.2 are amended to mandate physical, decentralized, hermetically isolated caches of Tier-4 and Tier-5 critical spare capital—specifically solid-state power switches, RO membranes, optical transceivers, and transformer cores—held in common stock beneath every bioregional microgrid, sized for a minimum continuous operating duration of thirty-six (36) months of unassisted islanding.

2. **Tactical Paralysis of Peace Guilds Under Armed Infiltration (Art. 8.1.2):**
   - *Vulnerability:* Civic Peace Guilds were constitutionally confined to non-lethal, somatic physical de-escalation and bare-handed restraint. Concurrently, automated point-defense (Art. 8.1.4) was restricted exclusively to inbound airborne/ballistic projectiles. Covert, armed saboteurs infiltrating municipal conduits (sewers, sub-aqueducts, sensor shafts) exploited this procedural gap: Peace Guilds could not legally neutralize armed combatants with lethal or stand-off energy force, while automated systems could not engage dismounted targets inside civil conduits.
   - *Mechanical Fix:* Article 8.1.2 is amended to instantiate the *Infrastructure Defense Cohort* (a rotating, sortition-selected, technically certified detachment of the Civic Peace Guild). When armed kinetic breach of vital life-support arteries (Class-A infrastructure) is sensor-verified, the Cohort is procedurally authorized to unlock localized, kinetic, and directed-energy containment equipment strictly inside the spatial bounds of the compromised conduit. The mandate remains strictly non-punitive: neutralizing physical threats to infrastructure life-support without creating standing police or carceral organs.

3. **Supermajority Deadlock & Stand-off Electronic/Sensor Drift (Art. 8.1.4 & Art. 9.6.2):**
   - *Vulnerability:* The 80% Black-Sky autonomous defense threshold created an impossible quorum requirement during active electronic warfare (EW), jamming, or atmospheric optical degradation (FSO loss), paralyzing defensive response against ambiguous or sub-ballistic kinetic incursions.
   - *Mechanical Fix:* Article 8.1.4 is amended to introduce a *Graduated Escalatory Defense Framework* (Tier-1 Proportional Interception at 60% localized quorum; Tier-2 Active EW/Directed Counter-Battery at 70%; reserving Tier-3 Fully Autonomous Kinetic Area Denial for the 80% threshold). Article 9.6.2 is reinforced by establishing multi-spectral, hardwired underground galvanic and seismic consensus rings that bypass jammed or attenuated free-space optical networks, preventing artificial consensus starvation during grey-zone sieges.

